<title>USA: CNS backs analysts' estimates.</title>
<headline>CNS backs analysts' estimates.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>CNS Inc president Richard Jahnke said the company is comfortable with Wall Street analysts' earnings estimates in a range of $0.15 to $0.18 per share for the third quarter.</p>
<p>&quot;Certainly the range is right,&quot; Jahnke said in an interview Wednesday at a Dain Bosworth conference.</p>
<p>He also said estimates for 1996 earnings in a range of $0.73 to $0.80 per share were on target.</p>
<p>	   -- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
